<section class="section" id="for">
  <div class="section-header"><div class="section-number">05</div><h2>Boucle for — for classique, for…in, for…of</h2></div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <div class="explainer">
      La boucle <strong>for</strong> combine l'initialisation, la condition et l'incrément en une seule ligne.
      <strong>for…in</strong> itère sur les propriétés d'un objet.
      <strong>for…of</strong> itère sur les valeurs d'un tableau (ou itérable).
      Syntaxe : <code>for (init; condition; incrément) { ... }</code>
    </div>

    <div class="code-block"><span class="cm">// for classique :</span>
<span class="kw">for</span> (<span class="kw">let</span> <span class="var-c">i</span>=<span class="num">0</span>; <span class="var-c">i</span> < <span class="num">5</span>; <span class="var-c">i</span>++) {
  <span class="fn-c">console</span>.<span class="fn-c">log</span>(<span class="str">"itération "</span> + <span class="var-c">i</span>);
}

<span class="cm">// for...in sur un objet :</span>
<span class="kw">let</span> <span class="var-c">personne</span> = {prenom:<span class="str">"Ahmed"</span>, age:<span class="num">25</span>};
<span class="kw">for</span> (<span class="kw">let</span> <span class="var-c">cle</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="var-c">personne</span>) {
  <span class="fn-c">console</span>.<span class="fn-c">log</span>(<span class="var-c">cle</span> + <span class="str">": "</span> + <span class="var-c">personne</span>[<span class="var-c">cle</span>]);
}

<span class="cm">// for...of sur un tableau :</span>
<span class="kw">let</span> <span class="var-c">fruits</span> = [<span class="str">"pomme"</span>,<span class="str">"banane"</span>,<span class="str">"kiwi"</span>];
<span class="kw">for</span> (<span class="kw">let</span> <span class="var-c">fruit</span> <span class="kw">of</span> <span class="var-c">fruits</span>) {
